   "evidence": "ArtinMap.lean:166-167 proves `artinHomAway ... I = \u03c3` by `rw [artinHomAway_apply ..., finprod_eq_single _ v, hI, FractionalIdeal.count_self, zpow_one, artinElementAway_eq_of_isArithFrobAt ...]`; the intermediate value after `zpow_one` is exactly `artinElementAway hab S hur v`, and no lemma states it. `grep -n \"artinElementAway\" ArtinMap.lean` shows its only public facts are `_eq_one_of_mem` (94), `artinSymbol_eq_mk_artinElementAway` (99), `isArithFrobAt_artinElementAway` (110) and `_eq_of_isArithFrobAt` (125), none mentioning `artinHomAway`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/NumberTheory/NumberField/Ideal/ArtinMap.lean",
   "fix": "Add `theorem artinHomAway_apply_eq_artinElementAway (I : idealsAway S) (v) (hv : v \u2209 S) (hI : ((I : (FractionalIdeal (\ud835\udcde K)\u2070 K)\u02e3) : FractionalIdeal (\ud835\udcde K)\u2070 K) = (v.asIdeal : FractionalIdeal (\ud835\udcde K)\u2070 K)) : artinHomAway hab S hur I = artinElementAway hab S hur v`, which is the first three rewrites of the current proof of `artinHomAway_apply_prime`, and derive `artinHomAway_apply_prime` from it via `artinElementAway_eq_of_isArithFrobAt`.",
   "issue": "The only prime-value lemma, `artinHomAway_apply_prime`, requires the caller to supply `Q` above `v` and `\u03c3` with `IsArithFrobAt`, even though the value is `artinElementAway hab S hur v` outright. The link between the file's two main objects is therefore missing, and callers must redo the finprod computation from `artinHomAway_apply` or re-derive a Frobenius witness \u2014 the PR itself does the latter twice, at lines 192-193 and 234-235.",
